  "description": "It was supposed to be a one-night stand born out of pure desperation, a reckless gamble to throw her ex's betrayal back in his face. Instead, her entire scheme was exposed before the sun even rose. But rather than using her failed plot as blackmail, the dangerously alluring stranger makes a cool, unexpected offer. Putting a contract on the table, he fixes his dark eyes on her and whispers his term: \"Two months. Just like last night.\" Bound by a steamy, perilous deal with a man who holds all the cards, she steps into a perilous game of passion and power. As the boundaries between calculated vengeance and consuming desire blur, one question remains: can this relationship truly end in revenge, or will she burn in the fires she lit?\n\n(Source: Lezhin US)\n\n*Note: Includes one extra chapter.*",
